    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2JSqYguSA89d1Vi3WN6ZEXp)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- `Mentions` in `sp-grouped-backlinks` is now a section with one subsection per kind of source note:\n  - **Notes**: regular notes (tagged `concept` or `zettel`; untagged notes land here too so no mention is dropped).\n  - **Litnotes**: notes tagged `litnote`.\n  - **Writing projects**: files below `sp-writing-projects`; this wins over the tags.\n- Empty kinds are not shown; meta-key groups (e.g. `pub-author`) are unchanged.\n- More padding between blocks: new `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks-block-padding` (default 2 blank lines) read by the Org buffer, the sidebar and the `vulpea-ui` widget.\n- All three views share `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks-sections` and the existing faces.\n- Docs edited in `docs/tangles/vulpea/sp-vulpea.org` (bullet lists); the two `.el` files are the matching tangles. No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Not run: no Emacs in the cloud container (checked paren balance only). New and updated ERT tests are in `tests/sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks-test.el`; please run them and try the sidebar on a note with litnote and writing-project mentions.\n- `.org` and `.el` code blocks were compared and are identical.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9QYSBU3buMw6s8NW1)_",
